         <manifestation label="" xml:id="source_d1e82">
            <titleStmt xml:id="titleStmt_N20327">
               <title xml:id="title_364N200B4">Score, doubtful autograph, fair copy</title>
            </titleStmt>
            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_N2032D">
               <titlePage label="Title page" xml:id="titlePage_364N200C4">
                  <p xml:id="idm58">Above the first stave: "Collect / Til Julefesten 1847. componeret af J:P:E: Hartmann. d 4 Novbr 1847."</p>
               </titlePage>
               <extent xml:id="extent_N20333">2 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_N20336">27.5 x 34</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_N20339">Paper: 20 staves.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
            <notesStmt xml:id="notesStmt_N2033B">
               <annot type="source_description" xml:id="annot_364N200D3">
                  <p xml:id="idm64">This score was transferred from the vicar F.V. Andersen's collection of letters (DK-Kk NKS 4532 4º). On top of the manuscript he has written: "Hartmanns eget Manuscript foræret mig af C. Rothe." (Hartmann's personal manuscript, donated to me by C. Rothe). Rothe was vicar at Vor Frue Kirke (Church of Our Lady) in Copenhagen where Hartmann was organist. It is, however, doubtful whether it is in Hartmann's hand. Contrary to Hartmann's habit the text is written in Latin script - not in Kurrent. It bears no resemblance to the autograph score mentioned above.</p>
               </annot>
            </notesStmt>
